{%- comment -%}
  fye-collection-guide — buying guidance below the product grid, from the
  collection's own `custom.buying_guide` metafield (rich text).

  Added 28/09/2026 (W450). Semrush's rankings showed six collections on pages
  5 to 8 of Google carrying about 130 words each, all of it in the intro band
  above the grid. The intro stays short on purpose, because it sits above the
  products; the depth goes here, after them, where it helps the shopper who
  has scrolled the grid and is still deciding.

  Content lives on the COLLECTION, not in this section's settings, because
  collection.json is one template shared by every collection: a setting here
  would print the same words on all of them. Edit it in Shopify admin under
  the collection > Metafields > Buying guide. A collection with an empty
  metafield renders nothing at all, so the section is safe on every
  collection.

  The copy is written to the never-sell-on-price rule: it argues from fit,
  durability and the finished result, never from a saving.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign guide = collection.metafields.custom.buying_guide
  assign band = s.band | default: 'ivory'
-%}

{%- if guide != blank -%}
<section class="cguide band band--{{ band }}" data-screen-label="Collection buying guide">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <div class="prose cguide__body">{{ guide | metafield_tag }}</div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
.fye .cguide__body :where(a) { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
.fye .cguide__body :where(h2, h3) { color: var(--ink); }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Collection buying guide",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "band", "label": "Background", "default": "ivory",
      "options": [
        { "value": "white", "label": "White" },
        { "value": "ivory", "label": "Ivory" },
        { "value": "mist",  "label": "Mist" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Collection buying guide" }]
}
{% endschema %}
